Short:        Rename multiple files
Author:       Uwe Rosner
Uploader:     u.rosner@ymail.com (Uwe Rosner)
Type:         util/misc
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.3
Distribution: Aminet


=====
ABOUT
=====
Tool for renaming selected files or directories according to specified masks. All source files/directories must be in the same directory. The following functions can be applied using the masks:

- Create a numbered file list 
- Convert to upper/lower case letters 
- Replace a specific text in the file name with another one
- Inserting the date/time of the file 
- Keep only certain letters of the file name 
- Mix all the masks above
- All of the above for name extension, too

MultiRename is based on the AmigaOS3.2.3(!) BOOPSI objects (Reaction) and therefore only runs on Amigas with this operating system or newer versions.

In fact, it utilizes a recently updated feature of ‘string.gadget’ from the latest AmigaOS update 3.2.3 from April 2025. Therefore, you must have at least this operating system version installed in order to run the tool properly.

